<h2>Project Intake</h2>
<p>The first step that all Webstar clients do before their project is fill out an intake form. The intake form gathers information crucial to the project like the business name, contact information, services required, and a general background about the business. Much of this information is discussed in the 1-on-1 consultation, so the intake was just for information needed to create the new website, transfer to Webstar hosting, and for photography services.</p>
<p>For this project, Steve needed a fully functional business website that showcased the work, with his chosen method of booking to be a contact form or a phone call. He also needed Google Maps, Yelp, and Apple Maps presence as well.</p>

<h2>Working on the Project</h2>
<p>In creating this project for Metro Detroit Holiday Lighting, the first step was discerning what in specific would set this business apart from other businesses in the same niche.</p>
<p>In holiday lights and other service industries that offer custom designs, the pictures is what sells the work. Crispy and color corrected pictures were what this site desperately needed. Then, a website that can showcase the service would be doable.</p>

<figure class="article-figure">
    <img src="<?php echo webstar_h($mdhlCaseStudyImg('mdhl-ranch-estates-1.webp')); ?>" alt="Metro Detroit ranch estate with wrapped tree, lit shrubs, and warm entry lighting at night" width="1280" height="854" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
</figure>

<p>Most of Metro Detroit Holiday Lighting's work only shows at night, with the exception of premium wreaths and garlands. Therefore the site should have a darker theme.</p>

<h2>Website Design</h2>
<p>In designing the feel of the site, I opted for a dark colorway to make the photos stand out and some light panels to accentuate daytime photos of wreaths and garlands. For the layout, clear panels with images give the user something to look at while they scroll and read. In general and with this business, people like to look at pictures more than they like to read.</p>

